From 25f9f21ef840f9d4286f4ac6c75759a9d02bb82f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max schwenk <maschwenk@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 03:10:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Answer empty object type checks from lazy member tables

isEmptyObjectType and the empty object test in removeSubtypes resolve a
lazy member table in full (every member instantiated) to learn that it has
properties. A type with a lazy member table is an instantiated reference,
never anyFunctionType, and the table has its signatures and index infos,
so isEmptyStructuredType answers from the table and otherwise does what
both sites did before.

38k-file program (37,942 files), tsgo on main + #64475 + #64526 + the
previous commit, median of 3, single threaded / 4 checkers: symbols
13,297,217 -> 13,082,184 (-1.6%) / 19,553,613 -> 19,241,821 (-1.6%),
types and instantiations unchanged, heap after check 10.47 -> 10.41 GB
(-0.5%) / 15.41 -> 15.32 GB (-0.6%).

Prototype in a Rust port of the checker (same counts as this commit):
30,572 empty object queries answered by a table single threaded, -215K
symbols (-1.6%), -268K with 4 checkers (measured on the tuple commit
without the others), peak -0.04 GB.

lazyMembersEmptyObjectType.ts covers subtype reduction of array literals
mixing primitives with empty and non-empty generic interfaces and classes,
assignability to empty interfaces and spreads. Baselines are generated on
main without #64475 and #64526.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
